= References

== Purpose

This section contains technical specifications and detailed reference documentation for Ceradoc.

== Overview

References are organized by topic:

=== API References

* link:/ceradoc/references/api-reference/[API Reference] - Complete API documentation
* link:/ceradoc/references/ruby-methods/[Ruby Methods Reference] - Ruby API methods reference
* link:/ceradoc/references/coremodel-types/[CoreModel Types] - CoreModel type definitions

=== Syntax Guides

* link:/ceradoc/references/asciidoc-syntax/[AsciiDoc Syntax] - AsciiDoc authoring guide
* link:/ceradoc/references/markdown-syntax/[Markdown Syntax] - Markdown authoring guide

=== Tools Reference

* link:/ceradoc/references/cli-commands/[CLI Commands] - Command-line interface reference
* link:/ceradoc/references/error-codes/[Error Codes] - Error codes and recovery strategies
* link:/ceradoc/references/feature-matrix/[Feature Matrix] - Feature support across formats

=== Model and Extensions

* link:/ceradoc/references/model-classes/[Model Classes] - All model classes catalog
* link:/ceradoc/references/model-bindings/[Model Bindings Table] - Grammar rule -> model table schema
* link:/ceradoc/references/output-formats/[Output Formats] - Format options and converters
* link:/ceradoc/references/extension-points/[Extension Points] - Extension API specification

== Reference Structure

Each reference provides:

* **Specification** - Formal definition
* **Parameters** - Method/class parameters
* **Returns** - Return types and values
* **Raises** - Exceptions that may be raised
* **Examples** - Usage examples
* **Notes** - Important considerations

== When to Use References

* **API Reference** - Look up method signatures and parameters
* **Model Classes** - Find model class inheritance and attributes
* **Output Formats** - Understand format options
* **Extension Points** - Learn extension APIs

== Related Documentation

* link:/ceradoc/pages/[Core Pages] - Conceptual documentation
* link:/ceradoc/tutorials/[Tutorials] - Step-by-step learning
* link:/ceradoc/guides/[Guides] - Task-oriented guides
